      "reasons": [
       "native TES3Merge merges the garbage in AIDT padding: it writes four creature records that change nothing, and copies the padding into the ones both write",
       "native TES3Merge writes MGEF subrecords in TES3Lib's property order, sounds after the description, not the order of the Construction Set, OpenMW, and every source plugin; the reordered bytes differ from the original, so it writes three magic effects that change nothing",
       "native TES3Merge keeps a cell's NAM0, the count of the temporary references after it, when it comes before the first reference, and then leaves every reference out; the port writes no count for references it doesn't write, and OpenMW's engine never reads it"
